(gen_random_uuid(), 'deprosc-nepal-nuwakot-rasuwa-vacancies-20261026', 'global', 'Nepal',
'DEPROSC-Nepal Hiring for Nuwakot and Rasuwa Field Roles: Apply by 28 October 2026',
'नुवाकोट र रसुवाका फिल्ड पदका लागि डिप्रोक्स–नेपालमा भर्ना: २८ अक्टोबर २०२६ सम्म आवेदन दिनुहोस्',
'DEPROSC-Nepal is hiring for six groups of field roles in Nuwakot and Rasuwa districts for response and early recovery projects funded by Plan International Nepal and ShelterBox, and applications close at 5:00 pm on 28 October 2026. Roles cover a project officer, engineers and overseers, programme assistants, a finance officer, a child protection officer and a relationship officer.',
'डिप्रोक्स–नेपालले नुवाकोट र रसुवा जिल्लाका लागि प्लान इन्टरनेसनल नेपाल र सेल्टरबक्सको सहयोगमा सञ्चालित प्रतिकार्य तथा प्रारम्भिक पुनर्लाभ परियोजनामा छ समूहका फिल्ड पदमा भर्ना खुलाएको छ र आवेदन दिने अन्तिम मिति २८ अक्टोबर २०२६ साँझ ५:०० बजे हो।',
$$<p><a href="https://deprosc.org.np/careers/">DEPROSC-Nepal</a> is hiring for six groups of field roles in Nuwakot and Rasuwa districts, and applications close at 5:00 pm on Wednesday, 28 October 2026. The roles support response and early recovery projects in Rasuwa, Nuwakot and Dhading, funded by Plan International Nepal and ShelterBox, the announcement on the organisation's own careers page said. <a href="https://merorojgari.com/job/deprosc-nepal-kathmandu-rasuwa-nuwakot-full-time-project-officer-engineer-overseer-program-assistant-finance-officer-child-protection-officer/">Nepali job boards carried the full announcement</a> on 26 October 2026, so candidates have two days to apply. The announcement asks for applications within seven days or by 28 October 2026 at 5:00 pm; work to the absolute date.</p>
<h2>At a glance</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Organisation</th><td>Development Project Service Centre (DEPROSC-Nepal)</td></tr>
<tr><th>Projects</th><td>Response and early recovery in Rasuwa, Nuwakot and Dhading, funded by Plan International Nepal and ShelterBox</td></tr>
<tr><th>Locations</th><td>Field offices in Nuwakot and Rasuwa; programme work in Galchhi, Kispang and Uttargaya</td></tr>
<tr><th>Roles</th><td>Project Officer (1), Engineer/Overseers (few), Program Assistants (2/3), Finance Officer (1), Child Protection Officer (1), Relationship Officer (1)</td></tr>
<tr><th>Deadline</th><td>5:00 pm on Wednesday, 28 October 2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>How to apply</th><td>Email contact@deproscnepal.org or post to DEPROSC-Nepal, P.O. Box 10953, Kathmandu</td></tr>
<tr><th>Documents</th><td>Cover letter, photograph, updated CV with two referees, other credentials</td></tr>
<tr><th>Salary</th><td>Not stated</td></tr>
<tr><th>Not stated</th><td>Exact total posts, salary, contract length, start date, stages beyond shortlisting</td></tr>
</table>
<h2>Why it matters</h2>
<p>These are field posts, not Kathmandu desk jobs. The stations are the field offices in Nuwakot and Rasuwa and the working municipalities of Galchhi, Kispang and Uttargaya. Local knowledge and a valid two-wheeler licence recur as preferences: the successful candidates will travel daily to project sites. A candidate living near the project districts, who can already ride to field sites, starts with a clear advantage.</p>
<p>One announcement covers the full shape of a field project: a project officer to lead work, engineers for drinking-water schemes, programme assistants for community activities, a finance officer for field-level money, a child protection officer for stakeholder work, and a relationship officer for government coordination. A candidate who does not fit one role may fit another, and all six groups share the same deadline.</p>
<h2>Roles on offer</h2>
<p>The Project Officer (1 post) in Nuwakot will lead an adolescent-responsive project improving access to accurate sexual and reproductive health information and services. It needs a bachelor's degree in a relevant discipline and three years of proven experience; female candidates with local knowledge will be preferred.</p>
<p>The Engineer/Overseers (a few posts) in Nuwakot and Rasuwa will survey, design, estimate and implement drinking-water schemes. They need a bachelor's degree in civil engineering with one year of proven experience; local knowledge and a two-wheeler licence will be preferred.</p>
<p>The Program Assistants (2 or 3 posts) in Galchhi, Kispang or Uttargaya will facilitate Cash for work, Cash for livelihood, WASH, Shelter and sexual and reproductive health activities. The routes in are a bachelor's degree in any discipline, or a 10+2 qualification, preferably in enterprise development, Cash for work or early recovery, with three years of social mobilisation experience. Residents of the project locations with a valid two-wheeler are encouraged to apply.</p>
<p>The Finance Officer (1 post) in Nuwakot will manage all project finance at the field office under the central office in Thapathali, Kathmandu. It needs a bachelor's degree in a relevant discipline and three years of proven experience; residents of the project districts with a two-wheeler licence will be prioritised.</p>
<p>The Child Protection Officer (1 post) in Rasuwa, with frequent field visits, will work closely with local stakeholders on the protection theme in line with Plan's priorities. It needs a bachelor's degree in a relevant discipline and two years of proven experience; female candidates from the project districts with a two-wheeler licence will be prioritised.</p>
<p>The Relationship Officer (1 post) in Nuwakot will work closely with the National Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Authority, Bidur municipality and other stakeholders, and may be deputed to other government offices on request. It needs a bachelor's degree in a relevant discipline with good exposure to software-based work; candidates from the project districts will be prioritised.</p>
<h2>Who should apply</h2>
<p>Every role except the programme assistant route asks for a bachelor's degree plus one to three years of experience, while that route opens a door for 10+2 graduates with three years of social mobilisation experience. Women and candidates from disadvantaged communities are highly encouraged to apply, the organisation said. State plainly where you are based and whether you hold a valid two-wheeler licence.</p>
<h2>How to apply</h2>
<ol>
<li>Pick one role that matches your qualification, experience and station; the six groups differ, so applying for the wrong group wastes the short window.</li>
<li>Prepare a cover letter, a recent photograph, an updated CV naming two referees, and copies of your credentials, including degree certificates and proof of experience.</li>
<li>Send the application by email to contact@deproscnepal.org, or by post to DEPROSC-Nepal, P.O. Box 10953, Kathmandu. Email is the safer route this late in the window, because a postal application may not arrive by 5:00 pm.</li>
<li>Keep proof that you sent it: a sent-email copy or a postal receipt. The announcement gives no tracking system.</li>
<li>Wait for contact. The organisation said only shortlisted candidates will be contacted. Canvassing or trying to influence the process will automatically cancel an application, the announcement said.</li>
</ol>
<h2>What is not stated</h2>
<p>Several details a candidate would normally want are simply not in the announcement, and they should not be guessed. The careers page gives the number of vacancies only as "several": the stated figures add up to at least seven posts plus a few engineers and overseers, but the exact total is not published. No salary, contract length or start date is stated, and no examination or interview schedule is given beyond shortlisting.</p>
<h2>Apply safely</h2>
<p>The announcement names no application fee and no agent. Anyone who asks for payment to submit an application, arrange shortlisting or secure one of these posts is not acting for the organisation. The only genuine routes published are the email and postal addresses above, and the only place to verify the vacancy is the careers page at <a href="https://deprosc.org.np/careers/">deprosc.org.np/careers</a>, which lists the same roles and deadline.</p>$$,
$$<p><a href="https://deprosc.org.np/careers/">डिप्रोक्स–नेपाल</a>ले नुवाकोट र रसुवा जिल्लाका लागि छ समूहका फिल्ड पदमा भर्ना खुलाएको छ र आवेदन दिने अन्तिम मिति बुधबार, २८ अक्टोबर २०२६ को साँझ ५:०० बजे हो। यी पद रसुवा, नुवाकोट र धादिङमा सञ्चालित प्रतिकार्य तथा प्रारम्भिक पुनर्लाभ परियोजनाका लागि हुन्, जसलाई प्लान इन्टरनेसनल नेपाल र सेल्टरबक्सले आर्थिक सहयोग गरेका छन्, संस्थाको आफ्नै करियर पृष्ठमा रहेको विज्ञापनले भनेको छ। <a href="https://merorojgari.com/job/deprosc-nepal-kathmandu-rasuwa-nuwakot-full-time-project-officer-engineer-overseer-program-assistant-finance-officer-child-protection-officer/">नेपाली जब बोर्डहरूले पूरा विज्ञापन</a> २६ अक्टोबर २०२६ मा प्रकाशित गरे, त्यसैले उम्मेदवारसँग आवेदन दिन दुई दिन मात्र छन्। विज्ञापनले सात दिनभित्र वा २८ अक्टोबर २०२६ साँझ ५:०० बजेसम्म आवेदन मागेको छ; ठ्याक्कै मितिलाई नै आधार मान्नुहोस्।</p>
